# USB control channel, see usb-gadget.sh.
# gser (default): two bulk-only serial functions per controller, no interrupt endpoint and no
#   network. Interface 0 carries the journal (read by the M1's bulk-log reader), interface 1 a
#   raw byte pipe with sshd on it (the M1's usb-pipe is ssh's ProxyCommand). Web access comes
#   through the M1's CONNECT proxy, reverse-forwarded by that SSH session (/etc/environment).
# ecm, ncm or eem: a CDC network function instead (macOS 26.0.1 loads ECM; no usable EEM
#   driver), SSH on 10.66.0.2:22. ACM=1 puts a CDC-ACM journal port in front of it. Both ECM
#   and ACM add an interrupt endpoint, after which attempt 18's device stopped answering.
FUNCTION=gser
ACM=0
